  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote the endless runner in `src/main.ts`. `typecheck` passes. I couldn't run `vite build` or open the game in a browser, so none of it has been run: the rendering, the jump and collision feel, and the `frame.dt` units (assumed to be seconds) are all unchecked.\n\n- **Scene:** Aura3D with the `outdoor-day` look. The runner stays at the origin and the world scrolls toward the camera. The runner is built from boxes and a sphere, with swinging legs and arms, a tucked jump pose and a blob shadow. Scenery is a pool of recycled nodes: center dashes, cross stripes, side posts and trees.\n- **Hurdles:** The first hurdle appears at 28 m, then heights run 0.4–1.15 m with gaps of 1.15–2.35 s of travel time. They come from a seeded generator (mulberry32), so a given seed repeats. The default seed is fixed and `?seed=N` overrides it.\n- **Physics:** Jumping uses a gravity arc (gravity 30, jump velocity 11, so a 2 m apex) and can't be repeated in the air. Speed is 10 m/s plus 0.02 m/s per meter, reaching 20 m/s at 500 m. Hitting a hurdle sets `lost`. Reaching 500 m sets `won`.\n- **Input:** Space, ArrowUp, W and pointer click/tap jump. The first jump input starts the run from `ready`. R restarts.\n- **Restart behavior:** R, or a jump input after the run ends, returns to `ready` at 0 m, and the next jump input starts the run. The task text didn't say whether a jump input after the run ends should go straight to `playing`, so I chose `ready`.\n- **HUD:** DOM elements positioned over the top of the canvas show distance, session best and status. An overlay shows start and game-over (or win) text with a restart hint.\n- **Hooks:** `window.__TASK_STATE__` updates every frame and on input. `window.__TASK_READY__` is set one animation frame after the first frame callback.\n\n",
